{"file": "design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md", "line": 3, "before": "(the maker files are exported from the inside model v7)", "after": "(the maker files are exported from the inside model v9)", "follows": "model v9 (model-v9-notes.md section k)"}
{"file": "design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md", "line": 6, "before": "A 0.3 mm skin of skin-safe resin that closes", "after": "A 0.3 mm skin of resin (Master Bond EP30Med) that closes", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'liner resin (item 36, material)' 2026-11-13 04:15"}
{"file": "design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md", "line": 12, "before": "Default, to confirm with the maker: a skin-safe cast resin. The resin grade is open: the maker proposes one with its skin-contact certificate (open point 1).", "after": "Master Bond EP30Med: two parts, low viscosity, cures at room temperature, stated by its maker to meet ISO 10993-5 and USP Class VI (maker's guide, page 12). ISO 10993-5 is a cell-toxicity test, not a skin-wear test: no skin claim is made for version 1. Its viscosity and cure time are only in a sheet that could not be downloaded: the test strip of item 36 shows whether it fills 0.075 mm, and the cell's temperature is measured during the first cure (limit 45 degrees C).", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'liner resin (item 36, material)' 2026-11-13 04:15"}
{"file": "design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md", "line": 15, "before": "The cell is live during the cure and must not exceed its limit: Grepow answers the limit (K-A8). Whether the ribbons can float 0.075 mm inside a single cast, or the liner must be made as a laminate first, is open (K-A5, S19, B8). Repair after casting is not possible (B8).", "after": "The cell is live during the cure and must not exceed 45 degrees C (specs/cell.md, Requirements on the cell; K-A8). Whether the ribbons can float 0.075 mm inside a single cast, or the liner must be made as a laminate first, is open (K-A5, S19, B8); the liner keeps 0.3 mm with 0.075 mm of resin on each side of a circuit, and before the first ring the builder casts one test strip (60 mm of the circuit stack in a 0.3 mm skin), cuts it and reads the resin on each face with a 10x loupe: at least 0.075 mm on each side and no void over copper (item 36). Repair after casting is not possible: a ring with a damaged liner is scrapped (B8, item 36).", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'item 36' 2026-11-13 03:56"}
{"file": "design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md", "line": 43, "before": "1. Resin grade, supplier, skin-contact certificate: the maker proposes.", "after": "1. Resin: Master Bond EP30Med (decided). Its skin-contact claim: none for version 1 (ISO 10993-5 is a cell-toxicity test). Viscosity and cure time: not in a saved sheet; the test strip of item 36 shows.", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'liner resin (item 36, material)' 2026-11-13 04:15"}
{"file": "design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md", "line": 45, "before": "3. Cure temperature and time, and what the cell and flex tails tolerate: the maker with Grepow.", "after": "3. Cure temperature and time, and what the flex tails tolerate: the maker. The cell never goes above 45 degrees C (specs/cell.md); the first cure measures it.", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'liner resin (item 36, material)' 2026-11-13 04:15"}
{"file": "design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md", "line": 50, "before": "The slot seal (with the motor window seal SEAL2 on US 7 to 9) and the dam DAM1 of the joystick pocket come BEFORE the cast (design/mfg/assembly/assembly.md steps 19 and 20; the sealant and the dam material are not chosen, open item S26).", "after": "The slot seal (with the motor window seal SEAL2 on US 7 to 9) and the dam DAM1 of the joystick pocket come BEFORE the cast (design/mfg/assembly/assembly.md steps 19 and 20); the sealant of the slots and of SEAL2 is 3M Scotch-Weld DP420 Black (item 45); the dam material is not chosen (open item S26).", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'item 45' 2026-11-13 03:56"}
{"file": "design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md", "line": 64, "before": "sealed from the channel side before the cast (step 19); inside model v8", "after": "sealed from the channel side with 3M Scotch-Weld DP420 Black before the cast (step 19; item 45); inside model v8", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'item 45' 2026-11-13 03:56"}
{"file": "design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md", "line": 65, "before": "US 7, 8 and 9 only; same sealant and same step as the floor slots, before the cast (17.27)", "after": "US 7, 8 and 9 only; same sealant (3M Scotch-Weld DP420 Black, 0.80 cubic mm per window, item 45) and same step as the floor slots, before the cast (17.27)", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'item 45' 2026-11-13 03:56"}
{"file": "design/mfg/specs/body.md", "line": 14, "before": "Titanium grade 5 (Ti-6Al-4V), machined from bar (architecture 17.29). Reason:", "after": "Titanium grade 5 (Ti-6Al-4V), bar to ASTM B348, machined from bar in one piece (architecture 17.29; lead-decisions.md row 'item 99'). The builder asks for the bar certificate and checks it: tensile strength at least 895 MPa, 0.2 percent proof at least 828 MPa, elongation at least 10 percent. Reason:", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'item 99' 2026-11-13 03:56"}
{"file": "design/mfg/specs/body.md", "line": 17, "before": "Default, to confirm with the maker: CNC machining from bar (multi-axis), one piece. Whether one piece can be machined, or the band must be turned and the block milled and joined, is open point 1 (architecture S13).", "after": "Fixed (item 99): CNC machining from bar (multi-axis), one piece, general tolerance ISO 2768-m. Whether a maker can machine it as one piece, or the band must be turned and the block milled and joined, is still asked of the maker: open point 1 (architecture S13).", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'item 99' 2026-11-13 03:56"}
{"file": "design/mfg/specs/body.md", "line": 20, "before": "The body is polished, then coated gloss black (PVD or DLC; the maker names the process). The glass seat and the microphone seats are masked or finished after coating: open point 4. Coating thickness and Ra: open point 4.", "after": "The body is polished, then coated gloss black with Oerlikon Balzers BALINIT DLC: black, 1 to 3 um thick, applied under 250 degrees C; it adds at most 0.003 mm per face, which the 0.10 mm bond gap of the joystick frame takes. The maker's brochure lists titanium alloys as coatable but its table does not show for which coating: colour, gloss and adhesion are checked on the first coated body (item 105). The bond faces are abraded and cleaned with isopropyl alcohol before bonding (item 106); the glass seat and the microphone seats are masked or finished after coating: open point 4. Roughness Ra: open point 4.", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'item 105' and 'item 106' 2026-11-13"}
{"file": "design/mfg/specs/body.md", "line": 23, "before": "Reason: the screen leaves 0.15 mm or less of clearance and the corner metal is thin.", "after": "Reason: the screen leaves 0.05 mm of clearance per side (as modelled; items 96 to 98) and the corner metal is thin.", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'items 96, 97, 98' 2026-11-13 03:56"}
