{"file": "design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md", "line": 102, "before": "7. The joystick opening relies on the switches' own rating (IP6X and IPX7) and the dam DAM1 for water; dam material and the stiffener material are open item S26 (assembly.md section 5).", "after": "7. The joystick opening relies on the switches' own rating (IP6X and IPX7) and the dam DAM1 for water; version 1 claims no water or dust rating (item 101; the build guide holds one optional test, 1 m of water for 30 minutes, then open and look: its result is recorded, it is not a pass line). Dam material is open item S26 (assembly.md section 5); the stiffener is polyimide, 0.10 (band-flex-tails.md).", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'item 101' 2026-11-13 03:56; model v8 stiffener"}
{"file": "design/mfg/specs/cover-glass.md", "line": 6, "before": "(model v5; assembly.md step 23, conflict K-A4; architecture 17.23, 17.24; open item S26). The tape is not chosen and its compressed thickness is unknown.", "after": "(model v5; assembly.md step 23, conflict K-A4; architecture 17.23, 17.24). SEAL1 is a ring of tesa 61305 double-sided film, 50 um (bond to glass 12.4 N/cm); its sheet states no value for coated titanium and none for water: on the first body a bond check after 24 hours, then a water spray test; version 1 claims no water rating (item 110).", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'item 110 (glass seal SEAL1)' 2026-11-13 04:15"}
