{"file": "design/mfg/assembly/assembly.md", "line": 165, "before": "- **Radio corner:** if adopted, the resin corner RC1 is bonded to the body here, on the planes X -10.6 and Y 2.05 (`design/mech/antenna/antenna-study.md:91`), with an adhesive no file names (section 5). Its top carries part of the glass seat (`design/mech/antenna/antenna-study.md:92`). The check adds the two bonded seams (section 4, row 9).", "after": "- **Radio corner:** the resin corner RC1 is cast on its own in Master Bond EP30Med (the liner's resin) and bonded to the body here, before the board goes in, on the planes X -8.60 and Y 2.05 (`design/mech/antenna/antenna-study.md:91`; before model v9 the plane was X -10.6), with an adhesive no file names (section 5). It is not poured with the liner: the two cavities are 5.10 mm apart with metal between, and RC1 forms part of the board cavity's walls and of the glass seat, so it must exist before the board and the glass are fitted. Its top carries part of the glass seat (`design/mech/antenna/antenna-study.md:92`). The check adds the two bonded seams (section 4, row 9).", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'resin radio corner RC1, how it is made' 2026-11-13 04:28; radio corner default 2026-11-13 00:39; model-v9-notes.md section m row assembly.md lines 62, 84, 158, 165, 270, 345, 376"}
{"file": "design/mfg/assembly/assembly.md", "line": 169, "before": "MEM1 and MEM2 to the body, each a disc of 2.0 mm, at most 0.10 thick, with its own adhesive ring, pressed into its seat from outside (`design/mech/mic-path/mic-path.md:73`, `design/mech/mic-path/mic-path.md:74`). No part is chosen yet (S23, `design/architecture.md:521`).", "after": "MEM1 and MEM2 to the body, each a disc of woven acoustic mesh, Saati Acoustex 010a (52 um thick), 2.0 mm across, bonded with a ring of tesa 61305 film (50 um; 2.0 mm outside, 1.0 mm bore), stack 0.102 mm, pressed into its 0.10 mm seat from outside (`design/mech/mic-path/mic-path.md:73`, `design/mech/mic-path/mic-path.md:74`). The builder cuts mesh and film with punches of 2.0 and 1.0 mm (item 73, `design/architecture.md:521`).", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'item 73' 2026-11-13 04:15"}
{"file": "design/mfg/assembly/assembly.md", "line": 175, "before": "### Step 12. Bond the two microphone gaskets on the pocket bottoms", "after": "### Step 12. Place the two microphone gaskets on the pocket bottoms", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'item 74': no adhesive"}
{"file": "design/mfg/assembly/assembly.md", "line": 177, "before": "- **Join:** GSK2 and GSK3 (foam rings OD 1.80, bore 1.00, adhesive on both faces) to the bottom of each floor pocket (`design/mech/mic-path/mic-path.md:70`), in the thickness chosen in step 3 for the board that goes into this body.", "after": "- **Join:** GSK2 and GSK3 (Nitto SCF foam rings OD 1.80, bore 1.00, no adhesive) laid on the bottom of each floor pocket (`design/mech/mic-path/mic-path.md:70`), in the thickness chosen in step 3 for the board that goes into this body; the microphone's lid holds each ring against the pocket floor.", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'item 74' 2026-11-13 04:15"}
{"file": "design/mfg/assembly/assembly.md", "line": 187, "before": "The bonding faces are degreased with isopropyl alcohol [PROPOSED: reason, the coated faces carry handling oil].", "after": "The bond faces are abraded and cleaned with isopropyl alcohol before bonding (3M sheet, surface preparation E; item 106). Measurement: 5 lap-shear strips of coated Ti-6Al-4V from the same coating batch, bonded and pulled; pass: the break is inside the adhesive, not at the coating; a break at the coating means the bond faces are masked before coating.", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'item 106 (adhesive on the black coating)' 2026-11-13 03:56"}
{"file": "design/mfg/assembly/assembly.md", "line": 233, "before": "No file names it: the design only names the need (bench item B8, `design/architecture.md:473`). [PROPOSED: a thick, non-flowing UV-curing dam material; reason, it must not run up into the block under the board, it is reached only from the channel, and it cures without heat next to the cell.]", "after": "The sealant is 3M Scotch-Weld DP420 Black, the adhesive that already bonds the joystick frame, mixed 2:1 by volume and put in with a 0.5 mm needle before the cast, 0.80 cubic mm per window (item 45; bench item B8, `design/architecture.md:473`); the motor is glued rigid in its pocket anyway. Check on the first printed body: cut through the window and see the fill reach the motor's back face with no void over 0.1 mm.", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'item 45 (motor window seal, US 7 to 9)' 2026-11-13 03:56"}
{"file": "design/mfg/assembly/assembly.md", "line": 249, "before": "The resin grade is open (`design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md:43`).", "after": "The resin is Master Bond EP30Med: two parts, low viscosity, cures at room temperature, stated by its maker to meet ISO 10993-5 and USP Class VI (a cell-toxicity test, not a skin-wear test: no skin claim is made for version 1); its viscosity and cure time are not in a saved sheet (`design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md:43`). Before the first ring the builder casts one test strip (60 mm of the circuit stack in a 0.3 mm skin), cuts it and reads the resin on each face with a 10x loupe: at least 0.075 mm on each side and no void over copper; the strip also shows whether the resin fills 0.075 mm (item 36).", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'liner resin (item 36, material)' 04:15; 'item 36' 03:56"}
{"file": "design/mfg/assembly/assembly.md", "line": 249, "before": "At the joystick the resin fills under the stiffener and a 0.1 mm strip on each side of the pocket along its length, where the 7.0 mm pocket is wider than the 6.8 mm channel (`design/architecture.md:795`, `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:255`), up to the dam.", "after": "At the joystick the resin fills under the stiffener, up to the dam; since inside model v8 the channel and the 7.0 mm pocket are the same width, so no 0.1 mm strip is filled beside the pocket (before v8 the channel was 6.8 mm, `design/architecture.md:795`, `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:255`).", "follows": "model-v9-notes.md section m row assembly.md line 250; band-liner.md line 62"}
{"file": "design/mfg/assembly/assembly.md", "line": 250, "before": "the band's two edge walls set the width 6.8 mm (`design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md:28`).", "after": "the band's two edge walls set the width 7.0 mm (6.8 mm before inside model v8, `design/mfg/specs/band-liner.md:28`).", "follows": "model-v9-notes.md section m row assembly.md lines 11, 250"}
