{"file": "design/mfg/assembly/assembly.md", "line": 265, "before": "The tape itself is not chosen and its compressed thickness is unknown (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:160`, K22; open item S26).", "after": "SEAL1 is tesa 61305 double-sided film, 50 um (bond to glass 12.4 N/cm; its sheet states no value for coated titanium and none for water; item 110); ADH1 is tesa 69404, optically clear, 100 um (item 96, rest; `design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:160`, K22). Measurement on the first body: bond check after 24 hours, then a water spray test; version 1 claims no water rating.", "follows": "lead-decisions.md row 'item 110' and 'item 96, rest' 2026-11-13 04:15"}
